(62, '1cb813e0-db55-4744-92e9-74694834cd09', '', '', '', 10, 'Gravelynn', 'Power Word: Shield Priest M+', '', '### OVERVIEW\nThis build is heavy into Power Word: Shield and Prayer of Mending. Superb heals, topping teammates instantly and quick!\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\nPros: \n\nBig Heals\n\nLots of insta-casts\n\nBig Absorbs for Power Word: Shield\n\nCons: \n\nHaven\'t found any honestly\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nStat prio - \n\nInt > SP > Spirit > Crit\n\n### NOTES\nFeel free to PM me if youre struggling with the build! Its been working for me VERY well', 'spell_holy_divinespirit', 1, 1785464542, 1785464542, 2, 4, 4, 0, 2),
(63, '471659d6-686c-4d0b-a16e-91b3ba2af1a7', '', '', '', 10, 'Maanis', 'Arch Necromancer Frozen North Pack', '', '### OVERVIEW\nThey watered this with the ichor of 36 nerubian lords. Sh*t so cold they\'ll be asking you "Which way to Icecrown?" Gamer this\'ll flatline your pacemaker and still keep you shambling. Nuclear levels of rime. Heart stopping, Necromancer kush. This stuff has diamonds on it so you know the lichbloom to gloomweed ratio is legendary. A whiff of this? Yeah, this is that nefarious grave-robbing glacier grass. This is straight out of Northrend. This is what resurrected Tupac and he\'s back for revenge.\n\nWIP\n\n### NOTES\nGrab you a skeletal mage for a pet. Works just like water elemental, but permanent.', 'Ability_Mage_ChilledToTheBone', 0, 1785469175, 1785469175, 2, 8, 3, 0, 0),
(64, '11ab6e1b-6528-4d9d-ab42-a8a65274bba1', '', '', '', 10, 'Prestigemax', 'MY FROST BUILD, WIP', '', '### OVERVIEW\nMY FROST BUILD, WIP', 'ability_ardenweald_priest', 0, 1785469917, 1785469917, 2, 8, 3, 0, 0),
(65, 'e863b010-903d-45b0-9b29-9cde1df29a51', '', '', '', 10, 'Xdlol', 'Classic Warrior+', '', '### OVERVIEW\nThis build turns the classic Warrior leveling experience into something much faster and more explosive. You retain the hard-hitting melee playstyle Warriors are known for, but gain built-in Windfury, powerful cooldown stacking, and exceptional AoE damage that lets you chain-pull packs with ease.\n\nThe build is straightforward to play but rewards good cooldown management. Keep your abilities on cooldown, prioritize weapon upgrades and Strength, and you\'ll cut through both questing and dungeon content with very little downtime. Whether you\'re fighting a single elite or a dozen mobs at once, this build has the tools to handle it efficiently from level 1 all the way to 60.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\nThis spec is excellent for leveling, offering massive AoE and strong single-target damage. It feels like a classic Warrior on steroids, tearing through both packs and bosses with ease.\n\nThe spec revolves around using your cooldowns effectively (see the macro below), and like most builds, it only gets stronger as you level and unlock more talents and gear.\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nYour biggest upgrades while leveling will always be your weapons. If you\'re using Heirlooms, this is much less of a concern, as you can comfortably wear the full set all the way to level 60.\n\nStrength is your primary stat and should always be your priority. Thanks to your talents and abilities, you\'ll naturally gain plenty of Critical Strike and Haste, making Strength by far your most valuable stat.\n\n### ROTATION\nOn AoE pulls, start by Charge-ing into the pack, then use Whirlwind to apply Rend to all nearby enemies. Follow up with Spear, Dragon Roar, and Bladestorm. Throughout the fight, hold down Cleave while using any abilities as they come off cooldown to maximize your damage.\n\nFor single-target encounters (such as bosses), start with Charge, then Whirlwind, Death Wish, and your Cooldown Macro (linked below). Follow up with Colossus Smash, Raging Blow, and Bloodthirst.\n\nAfter your opener, rotate Bloodthirst and Raging Blow while keeping Rend active if it falls off. Use Colossus Smash on cooldown, and cast Stormstrike whenever you\'re low on Rage to keep your rotation flowing smoothly.\n\n### MACROS\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast Avatar\n/cast Skull Banner\n/cast Bloodbath\n/cast Warcry\n/cast Recklessness\n/cast Gurubashi Rage \n\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast [@cursor] Champion\'s Spear\n\n### WEAKAURAS\nRage / Swing Timer\n\n### NOTES\nYou\'re essentially a classic Warrior with built-in Windfury, powerful cooldown stacking, and devastating AoE abilities. Keep your cooldowns rolling, don\'t let anything sit unused, and charge from pack to pack, spinning your way through everything in your path.', 'ability_warrior_innerrage', 0, 1785486790, 1785581552, 2, 8, 0, 0, 1),
(66, 'e3ef4781-0365-4e98-a759-3a92fc5867b6', '', '', '', 10, 'Headbanga', 'Shadow Rogue (punish the meta)', '', '### OVERVIEW\nMelee Rogue/DK. High dmg burst window, anti-caster toolkit.\n\nExcels in 1v1 or 2v2 environments. Not advised to be used in BGs much.\n\nMacros found below to ease up rotation.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\nPros:\n+Strong anti magic defenses\n+Decent physical dmg defenses\n+Lots of CC\n+Lots of gap closers\n+Extremely high burst (Dummy test 19second ~55k damage)\n+Very decent pressure outside of burst windows\n+Macroable\n\nCons:\n-High skill cap\n-needs lots of binds\n-Macros are not always so flexible\n-No immunities\n-No trinket + getting stunned is very punishable\n-Melee attacks mostly\n-No self heals\n-Weak stealth, have to play around being detected\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nAgi+pvp stats\n2 daggers or 1 dagger mainhand and 1 sword-offhand\n\n### ROTATION\nFish for a trinket, then use control like kidneyshot.\nExecute the burst macro or do it yourself.\nBig window:\nShadowstep + Ambush 6-7 times.\nDont spend Combo Points on anything else but maybe one stun if needed again. Just spam step+ambush\n\nSmall window normal ShadowDance:\nNormal control + ambushes and Ghostly Finish\n\n### CONSUMABLES\nMainhand Runne of Cinderglacier\noff-hand poison\n\n### MACROS\n{HT}showtooltip [mod:shift] Ghostly Finish; Ambush\n/cast [mod:shift] Cold Blood\n/cast [mod:shift] Ghostly Finish\n/stopmacro [mod:shift]\n/cast Warcry\n/cast Shadow Blades\n/cast Shadowstep\n/castsequence reset=target/15 Forbidden Technique, Ambush, Ambush, Ambush, Ambush, Ambush, Ambush, Ambush, Ambush, Ambush\n\n\n\nAfter your kidney just spam your keybind without pressing shift, at the end press shift and spam same button.\n\n### WEAKAURAS\nAmbush WA that just lights up when u have one available.\n\n### NOTES\nHighly adjustable towards when and how to put pressure.\n\nYou can reduce your shadow damage to increase your pressure overall. But generally you have problem with survailabity, and you need to kill them, before they kill you.\n\nFor any improvements please send a message.\n\nNote: Currently Frost Presence is bugged, and you need to use it manualyl every time after exiting stealth. You can keep Blood presence on, but its not as good as frost presence.\n\nIf someone can test Unholy presence might be better.', 'Ability_Throw', 2, 1785494950, 1785497211, 3, 8, 1, 0, 3),
(67, '8039491b-146b-47df-86e7-ca2129a70714', '', '', '', 10, 'Gutfor', 'Updated - Dungeon cleave monster M+ 20 Completed', '', '### OVERVIEW\nUpdates: [In the process of updating]\n\nThis build has cleared and farmed up to mythic +20. Top DPS with a simple rotation.\n\n--> If you have any questions at all feel free to message at any time <--\n\nMoved some talents around;\n\n- Shredding blows (24% ARP) <-- Insane OP on smaller packs\n- Optimized % damage talents\n- 9 Expertise talent\n- 0 Hit talents as I have it from gear now. If you are missing hit you can take points from shredding blows and put them into fervor (1% hit/1% crit in berserker stance)\n- Added Bloodthirst as a filler (Reset mechanic with 1 point feels great)\n- Avatar removed from 1 button macro and treated as a secondary cooldown. Use on trash or between DW/Avenging as they still stack.\n- Added expose armor\n- Added Skull banner (OP CD for m+)\n\nThis build now brings huge group buffs -> 10% AP / 5% Crit / Kings / Battle Shout\n\nNew Rotation:\n\nMaintain slice and dice 46% AS through death mark and using slice. If on cooldown you can trigger slice from sinister strike combo points.\n\nAOE -> Sweep, Divine storm, Whirlwind, Bloodthirst, Judgement, Sinister strike \n\nSingle Tagret -> Sweep, Divinestorm, Bloodthirst, Judgement, Whirlwind, Sinister strike\n\nIf you have combo points you can use expose armor or if slice duraction is full use a deaths mark into a 5 point expose for giga boss damage shred.\n\n\nMain abilities:\n\n- Sweep\n- Divine storm\n- Whirlwind\n- Cleave\n- Bloodthirst\n- Judgement\n- Sinister strike \n\nSecondary: \n\n- Mycelial Ring \n- Death Mark\n- Slice and dice\n\nMajor dps cooldowns:\n\n- Avatar\n- Avenging wrath\n- Deathwish \n\nThis build will rely on these interactions:\n\n- Cleave (Macro it into all of your abilities and spam)\n- Sweep (Triggers molten fury for huge aoe damage)\n- Divine storm (Resets on holy damage sometimes)\n- Death mark (Provides 5 combo points)\n- Slice and dice (This is refreshed on kill by the rogue talent)\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\n|cff1aff1a+Big damage with little buttons|r\n\n### ITEMIZATION\n- 8% hit\n- 26 Expertise rating\n\n\nHit -> Expertise -> Strength -> Attack power -> Crit -> ARP -> Haste \n\nYou want to avoid haste at all costs on gear it\'s low prio and almost a dead stat for us\n\n### ROTATION\nSweep -> Divine Storm -> Whirlwind -> Bloodthirst -> Judgement -> Sinister Strike\n\nPrioritze sweep for aoe clearing and divine storm resets.\n\nMacro Lightbound cleave into all of your abilities it\'s free damage\n\n### CONSUMABLES\nWe love strength and attack power\n\n### MACROS\n/cast lava sweep\n/startattack\n/cast Lightbound Cleave(Rank 5)\n\n/cast whirlwind\n/cast Lightbound Cleave(Rank 5)\n/startattack\n\n/cast divine storm\n/startattack\n/cast Lightbound Cleave(Rank 5)\n\n/cast judgement of wisdom\n/startattack\n/cast lightbound cleave(Rank 5)\n\nAIO CD\n\n/cast death wish\n/cast avenging wrath\n/use Bloodbath(Rank 3)\n/cast blood fury\n/cast Bloodbath\n\n### NOTES\nFeel free to change some talents and abilities around as needed for mythic +\n\nConsider kicks, stuns, freedom, dispel, etc\n\nOr add more damage talents if you want', 'SPELL_HOLY_AVENGINEWRATH', 15, 1785496456, 1786493369, 2, 8, 0, 0, 0),
(68, '638cccc5-7b58-4086-8815-0a926c3b1d19', '', '', '', 10, 'Veritas', 'CryoRanger', '', '### OVERVIEW\nBuilding a frost ranger healer... lets see if this works.', 'ability_ardenweald_hunter', 3, 1785498684, 1785498684, 1, 4, 4, 0, 0),
(69, 'a483dcaf-0b01-467b-955f-5504eba84727', '', '', '', 10, 'Seja', 'Frost Zap DMG', '', '### OVERVIEW\nCurrent frost zap build. Easy & and a lot of AoE and ST DMG. Become the top dmg in dungeons! Try it out, improve it with enchants or talents! This are currently the enchants i have found, freshly dinged 60. Just wanted to share this so you guys can check it out!\n\nJust go classic mage stat prio.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\nEasy build with a lot of dmg.', 'ability_bastion_hunter', 1, 1785502628, 1785502762, 2, 8, 3, 0, 0),
(70, '99771807-3cbe-4429-8401-40c706d49d72', '', '', '', 10, 'Armos', 'Armos Wolf NUKE 2.2', '', '### OVERVIEW\nlike the old one but this is just str, so....the wolfs basicly do 25% more dmg if you just go str gear/str mainstat', 'ability_worgen_darkflight', 0, 1785518492, 1785518492, 2, 8, 0, 0, 0),
(71, 'c1ae0a02-530e-4376-9b60-4c131a1d5d2c', '', '', '', 10, 'Feints', 'Shadow Bear', '', '### OVERVIEW\nqwerty', 'Ability_Ambush', 2, 1785526937, 1785526937, 2, 8, 0, 0, 0),
(72, '428bbadc-54dc-41ed-b2af-41dbec5f67d4', '', '', '', 10, 'Tyranastros', 'Tyr\'s AoE Ret for Leveling', '', '### OVERVIEW\nAn attempt at a less mana-hungry AoE Ret Pally. Mostly successful, but it is possible to go OOM with a lack of Arcane Concentration procs and replenishment procs.\n\nNote: Highly Dependent on 3 core MEs for highest damage output.\n1. Hour of Judgement\n2. Templar Slash\n3. Consecrated Weapon\n\nRecommended to use Heirlooms and run MS leveling. AoE focus build that benefits from a lot of targets, but is a bit lacking in Single Target damage and self-sustain.\n\nStart\'s off with Fire Blast to help chunk enemies as you start leveling. Helps with tagging and ranged pulling. But can be dropped in the teen levels.\n\nCheck rotation and Macro sections.\n\nUse Seal of Command in group content, and use Seal of Wisdom for mana regen, if needed.\nUse Shadow Resistance Aura in groups, else Concentration Aura so that mobs have less pushback against Templar\'s Slash.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\nPros:\n+ High AoE DPS\n+ Decent Burst from 40+\n\nCons:\n- Mediocre Single Target DPS\n- Lacks self-sustain. Can struggle to solo quest at higher levels.\n- Mana Hungry. Arcane Concentration talent helps, but only delays the inevitable OOM.\n\nChug Endless Manastorm Potion in Manastorms for mana regen. You\'ll need it occasionally.\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nRecommended:\nChampion\'s Heirlooms\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1339124:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion Herod\'s Helmet]|h|r\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1642950:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion Herod\'s Shoulder]|h|r\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1648677:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion\'s Deathdealer Breastplate]|h|r\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1339096:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion Herod\'s Belt]|h|r\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1339117:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion Herod\'s Legguards]|h|r\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1339103:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion Herod\'s Boots]|h|r\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1339110:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion Herod\'s Bracers]|h|r\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1339131:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion Herod\'s Gloves]|h|r\n|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1339084:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:50|h[Champion\'s Deathdealer Cloak]|h|r\n\nAny 2-handed melee heirloom\nAny heirloom Rings, Neck, Trinkets.\n\n### ROTATION\nST:\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:10312|h[Exorcism]|h|r with Art of War proc (Instant Cast)\nIf target is 20% or less HP: |cff71d5ff|Hspell:24275|h[Hammer of Wrath]|h|r + |cff71d5ff|Hspell:20661|h[Execute]|h|rx2\nMaintain |cff71d5ff|Hspell:20922|h[Consecration]|h|r\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:53408|h[Judgement of Wisdom]|h|r\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:53385|h[Divine Storm]|h|r\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:278742|h[Templar\'s Slash]|h|r\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:35395|h[Crusader Strike]|h|r\nFiller: \n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:11580|h[Thunder Clap]|h|r / |cff71d5ff|Hspell:907424|h[Dawn Smash]|h|r\n\nAoE:\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:282984|h[Hour of Judgement]|h|r\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:954903|h[Light\'s Hammer]|h|r\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:2814|h[Holy Wrath]|h|r\nMaintain |cff71d5ff|Hspell:20922|h[Consecration]|h|r\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:278742|h[Templar\'s Slash]|h|r ( This has 3 charges, I recommend weaving a cast between Consecration, Thunderclap, and Whirlwind)\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:11580|h[Thunder Clap]|h|r / |cff71d5ff|Hspell:907424|h[Dawn Smash]|h|r\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:1680|h[Whirlwind]|h|r / Whirling Light\n|cff71d5ff|Hspell:11608|h[Cleave]|h|r / |cff71d5ff|Hspell:907302|h[Lightbound Cleave]|h|r\n\n### MACROS\n{HT}showtooltip\n/castsequence reset=7 Judgement of Wisdom, Crusader Strike\n/cast Heroic Strike\n/startattack\n\nAoE Rotation:\n{HT}showtooltip\n/castsequence reset=combat/8 Consecration, Templar Slash, Thunderclap, Templar Slash, Whirlwind, Templar Slash\n/cast Cleave\n/startattack\n\nNote: Replace base skills with ME if  known (|cff71d5ff|Hspell:907424|h[Dawn Smash]|h|r for |cff71d5ff|Hspell:11580|h[Thunder Clap]|h|r, Whirling Light for |cff71d5ff|Hspell:1680|h[Whirlwind]|h|r, |cff71d5ff|Hspell:907303|h[Lightbound Cleave]|h|r for |cff71d5ff|Hspell:11609|h[Cleave]|h|r)\n\nAoE CDs:\n{HT}showtooltip\n/castsequence reset=combat/30 [@cursor] Light\'s Hammer, Holy Wrath\n\nBurn Phase (20% HP or less)\n{HT}showtooltip\n/castsequence reset=combat/3 Execute, Hammer of Wrath, Execute\n\nBurst (with Manastorm Pot)\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast Avenging Wrath\n/cast Sweeping Strkes\n/cast Manastorm: Reflex Booster\n\n### NOTES\nWith Art of War talent and Divine Reset Mystic Enchant, Exorcism and Divine Storm abilities will be available to cast at different intervals, and thus don\'t fit neatly into a 1-button rotation.\n\nIf you have WeakAuras, you can set up a tracker for Art of War and Arcane Concentration to tell you the best times to cast Exorcism, making it a free instant cast.', 'SPELL_HOLY_AVENGINEWRATH', 3, 1785538197, 1786512444, 1, 8, 1, 0, 1),
(73, '863f7b56-e106-4f50-b9ee-5c59e085ee25', '', '', '', 10, 'Yehlemihas', '冰奶', '', '### OVERVIEW\n输出奶，刚需35紫色魔咒冰冷医师', 'ability_ardenweald_paladin_winter', 1, 1785544471, 1785544471, 2, 4, 4, 0, 0),
(74, '02a060fe-d52c-4c15-a21b-ec809fa8516c', '', '', '', 10, 'Singularion', 'Tyrs Shadow Lock Leveling Build', '', '### OVERVIEW\nA shadow bolt focused warlock build that takes advantage of the Nightfall talent for instant-cast Shadow Bolt, and later Seed of Corruption.\nPivots into a focus on Wild Imps at later levels, as Wild Imps are crazy strong.\n\nThe build is very mana hungry. It is recommended to level via Mana Storms. Else, be prepared to drink on a regular basis. Conjured food, water, and refreshments go a long way in aiding regen in solo content and dungeons.\n\nYou can track Arcane Concentration / Clearcasting to efficiently use high-cost spells and minimize mana spent.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\n|cff1aff1a+High ST and AOE damage potential|r\n+Some CC Options\n+Minions. Void Walker can tank solo content with ease.\n+ Decent Burst with Voidborne + Icy Veins + Soul Harvest\n\n-Mana guzzler. Can go OOM on a long fight / boss fight.\n\n### ROTATION\nSolo:\nPull with Frost Bolt (macro with /petattack )\nApply  Corruption\nHand of Gul\'dan for Wild Imps\nSpam Shadow Bolt\nShadowfury / Frost Nova to CC close enemies.\nMarch of the Dead for a burst of damage. Aim at a wall or cliff. They can wander pretty far and aggro more stuff if you summon the undead in an open area.\n\nAoE in Dungeons / ManaStorms:\nMarch of the Dead and Breath of Sindragosa as Freecast AoE\n\nAt low levels, Shadow Artillery and chanel Rain of Fire.\n\nAt high leels:\nHand of Gul\'Dan\nShadow Artillery\nUse Seed of Corruption, alternating targets. in Manastorms, every other Seed of Corruption will be instant-cast due to Manastorm hase boost.\nShadowfury for some CC.\n\nBoss Rotation:\nDoT Sequence: Corruption > Shadow Word: Pain > Devouring Plague > Curse of the Elements\nBurst CDs: Soul Harvest, Icy Veins\nInferno\nHand of Gul\'dan\nSpam Shadow Bolt\nRe-apply DoTs and use Hand of Gul\'dan on CD\nIf the Boss is near or against a wall, face the wall with the boss in-between you and the wall, and use March of the Dead.\n\n### MACROS\nDot Sequence:\n{HT}showtooltip\n/castsequence Corruption, Shadow Word: Pain, Devouring Plague, Curse of the Elements\n/petattack\n\nBurst:\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast Soul Harvest\n/cast Icy Veins\n\nOthers:\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast [@cursor] Shadowfury', 'ability_demonhunter_netherbond', 0, 1785554778, 1786307054, 1, 8, 3, 0, 0),
(75, '3b2279cd-e94f-4738-8939-e638a9c08e30', '', '', '', 10, 'Kalaa', 'EZ', '', '### OVERVIEW\nEZ', 'ability_deathknight_necroticaura', 1, 1785557079, 1785557117, 1, 8, 1, 0, 0);
