(158, '817d0b7d-8831-4e76-afce-1a2c1f42f2e2', '', '', '', 10, 'Tulslaeh', 'Tuls\' PW:S - Raid Edition', '', '### OVERVIEW\nShielding the damaged heals them and reduces the cooldowns on everything that pushes out AoE Healing. Be prepared to watch your mana evaporate in real time.\n\nYou are welcome to message me in game if you see me around and have questions about this or other builds.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\n|cff1aff1a+Nearly everything you do is instant cast so you can keep up with pretty much every group|r\n+Absorbs can trivialize a lot of the damage spikes prevelant in raids and allow the healer(s) you\'re grouped with to focus on the more attritional damage\n+Your AoE cooldowns are quick (don\'t fall into elixer syndrome)\n\n-You can OoM yourself within a minute, you can\'t just mindlessly chain cast.\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nSpell Power > Spirit/Crit (in this version of the build, more on that below) > Int/Haste\n\n### ROTATION\nPW:S if Borrowed Time isn\'t up and you\'re going to cast anything else.\nLightwell or Halo should be prioritized based on if the fight calls for stacking or spreading, but both should be applied generously.\nAfter an AoE has been used, begin cycling in synchronize to help reduce their Cooldowns\nIn my groups raids, the range stack stays fairly tight, so I save Field Surgery for us, and leave lightwell in melee, but if you tend to stand in melee you may want to reverse that.\n\n### NOTES\nCreated with the requirment of Cleanse & Tremor totem, Bloodlust, and Mass DIspell.\n\n"Why Time Warp?" I just think its neat! also, I have a habit of blinking stupid places and this gives me an out.\n"Why Not Circle of Life?" The reverse Halo isn\'t bad in and of itself, but it lacks the healing boost buff that remains on targets (potentially an oversight by the devs so it could be changed in the future.)\n\nAs usual with my builds i\'ve dipped into a lot of mana return to try and stabalize what is a normally mana intensive archetype, these are to be swapped out with throughput talents and abilities as the gear availability advances.\n\nGeneral Swaps:\nDampen/amp magic and the Elemental wards for Evocate if you\'re mostly doing pugs with downtime between pulls, or have raids where you aren\'t chain pulling like my Raid leaders like to. Also portals, those are nice. (dampen magic has a usecase in mitigating magic damage taken, but thats rarely the break point unless you\'re doing ascended.)\n\nAoE Swaps:\nBloodlust &  Time warp -> Holy Nova & Holy Super Nova for a chunky heal that dispells. (Cycle with Field Surgery)\nBloodlust, Tyr\'s Deliverence & Boundless Salvation -> Prayer of Healing + Prayer of Preservation + Preservation (I would argue this should only be considered if your raid is struggling with AoE damage incoming, and would benefit from talent swaps to the PoH + Halo, this also introduces a regular cast time element.)\nBloodlust -> Circle of Healing or  Divine Star. (minimal build change, and maintains instant cast playstyle)\nTIme Warp - > Ebbing Tides Totem\n\nMana Swaps:\nManagem uncommon -> Light well healing increase\nMoonwell -> Light of Life, or Tyrs Deliverence (I favour starting with halo, and picking up Tyrs later)', 'Spell_Holy_BorrowedTime', 0, 1786158578, 1786162013, 2, 4, 4, 0, 1),
(159, '915484d2-c78b-48c9-b70f-96d24d6e4caf', '', '', '', 10, 'Nicodimus', 'Bulwark Avatar Tank & Clevage Flurry', '', '### OVERVIEW\nTank big AoE Pulls in Manastorm, Dungeons, Heroics, & Mythics with mobs stuck on you solid.   Use a sword and shield to survive with mitigation and avoidance.  Use the many many defensive cooldowns to pull through any situation.   Get instant que times and smash content with friends using fast paced play style that feels unstopable.                          Use flametongue weapon, Defensive Stance, Devotion Aura &  Charge into combat sword first and protect allys by taking the hits they cant survive.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\nGood mobility,  good cround control. Fun to play.  Never worry about mana !  Takes advantage of Rage and Energy resources.  Does not use combo point spenders,  or runes.               Good single target threat generation,  great multi target threat generation.    Pretty easy to heal for healers.     Untested on raid bosses, expected to perform well.\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nStrength, Stamina, block, dodge, parry, defense,    Some expertise and hit is in talents here. The threat generation seems good with single target coming from shield slam and devastate.      Most of the talents improve armor penetration or attack power, and very little spellpower is accumulated. So Voidbound Cleve and Flurry of Shadow  seem to perform slightly worse than Fan of Knives & Cleve.   Running under Path of Duality the magic bassed versions may perform better than the standard abilities.\n\n### ROTATION\nIts nice to macro Cleve or Voidbound Cleve to Fan of Knives or Flurry of Shadow.                Place vigilance on a high threat ally.  Flametongue weapon.                                 Multi Target Rotation:    Charge ->  Fan of Knives & Cleve macro  ->  Thunder Clap ->  Shockwave  ->  get oriented and Bulwark !                                    Single Target Rotation:  Charge-> Shield Slam -> Devastate -> Revenge -> Riposte ->   Avatar or Stormcloak or Abyssal Ward or Evasion or Golem Form or Enraged Regeneration or Spell Reflection or Shield Block or Shield Slam.    Its situational.  Its fun.  Its fast. Its not boring.\n\n### CONSUMABLES\nStamina is life.\n\n### MACROS\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast Cleave\n/cast Fan of Knives\n\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast Voidbound Cleave\n/cast Flurry of Shadow\n\n### NOTES\nThere are some alternative options for Mystic Enchants like, First to the Fight, Shield of the Emperor, Rock Barrier, Mountain Fury. It would be nice to take Soul Link but then you have pet management.  It would be nice to have aspect of the Monkey but it takes a lot of junk to get it. There are lots of paladin talents in protection, but they didnt seem to provide any better avoidance or mitigation.', 'ability_warrior_stalwartprotector', 0, 1786165110, 1786165110, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0),
(160, '9191ed47-777d-49b0-bd82-4fe7fc7573cf', '', '', '', 10, 'Maellas', 'Blood Knight - Shield Tank', '', '### OVERVIEW\nPlays like a deathknight and avoids attacks like a shield tank, you only need to apply diseases and spam death strike and pestilence.\n\nOther important cooldowns will reduce damage significantly for a short while, while your voidwalker redirects damage to itself.\n\nDepending on the size of the pull and your parry, you can heal 54% to 162% of your max health every 10 seconds while bloodworms support you over time.\n\nAs for stats, you want warrior block tank gear for maximum mitigation with a focus on defense and block rating over block value.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\nPros:\n +Smooth-brain threat and capable of soloing a lot of things.\n +Dealing magic damage heals your pet and your pet can grab threat for you.\n +Powerful cooldowns that can be used strategically or simultaneously for increased \n   survivability and threat aquisition.\n +Receives 20% increased healing from all sources, including your own.\n\nCons:\n -Not a lot of options for breaking out of crowd control.\n -Beginning combat, you will need to apply your diseases to at least 1 target to receive the most \n  self healing.\n\n### NOTES\nI\'m new to level 60 classic content and even more new to seasonal specific changes, as this is my first time playing one.\nI\'ll slowly update this archetype page as I learn more.', 'ability_warlock_baneofhavoc', 1, 1786187265, 1786187265, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0),
(161, 'bf993799-5e44-4893-9588-eb70dacdfc3f', '', '', '', 10, 'Haruka', 'Healing Rain', '', '### OVERVIEW\nHow to play:\n\nCast Riptide.\nCast Healing Wave.\nCast Healing Rain.\nRepeat.\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nSP=Intellect>Crit>Haste\n\n### ROTATION\nRiptide on Cooldown, Healing Wave as filler, when on 5 stacks of Tidewaters, cast Tidal Force and immediately cast Healing Rain. Repeat.', 'spell_animabastion_groundstate', 0, 1786187776, 1786187776, 2, 4, 4, 0, 0),
(162, '3286b620-b4a0-48f0-a52e-986ef20115fb', '', '', '', 10, 'Morg', 'bleeding 5k damage (no finish yet full build)', '', '### OVERVIEW\nSimple build: bleed with critical hits to deal a lot of AoE damage and single target', 'ability_garrosh_hellscreams_warsong', 1, 1786198932, 1786198932, 2, 8, 0, 0, 1),
