(169, '492105df-4c17-401f-b9fe-47e21dd6e887', '', '', '', 10, 'Vuhjin', 'Vuhjin - Shadow Hunter', '', '### OVERVIEW\nI created this build with the intention of having fun with the Shadow Hunter archetype; I’ve always really liked Trolls, and unfortunately, Blizzard never released the Shadow Hunter class—and even the version in *Heroes of the Storm* doesn\'t really capture the lore-friendly archetype of the class.\n\nSurprisingly, even though it’s a "just for fun" build, it turned out to be extremely strong, so I’m sharing it for anyone who wants to use it.\n\nThe focus of this class is a sort of battle-mage; the Shadow Hunter in the lore would typically rely on *Curse of Agony*, but to take advantage of synergies, I used *Corruption*—I think it still fits the class lore quite well.\n\nCertain talents and mystic enchants are essential; the idea here is to proc *Nightfall* and *Maelstrom* as much as possible.\n\nI left out one skill—*Hex*—sacrificing it for *Water Walking* because I really enjoy walking on water, haha. But feel free to pick up *Hex*, as that would be the "correct" skill for a Shadow Hunter.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\n|cff1aff1a+ Pros|r\nMassive AoE damage\nHigh survivability\nHigh single-target damage\nGood kill speed\nNo downtime\nCompletely self-sufficient\n\n\n- Cons\nChugs mana like crazy\nLacks good AoE until level 40\nDependent on Mystic Enchants\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nI use a lot of haste, spell power, and agility.\n\n### ROTATION\nCorruption\n\nSpread to all targets using Sinister Strike.\n\nDrop Magma Totem and Stun Totem if there are multiple targets; switch to Windfury after the stun.\n\nWave of Despair whenever available.\n\nMeditation whenever you have 5 combo points, or Slice and Dice.\n\nBurn procs whenever available, prioritizing Seed of Corruption for multiple targets and Shadow Bolt for single targets.\n\n### MACROS\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast Void Strike\n/cast Cleave\n\n\n\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast Chain Lightning\n/stopcasting\n/startattack\n\n\n{HT}showtooltip Charge\n/cast Corruption\n/cast Charge\n\n\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast Shadow Waste Bolt\n/stopcasting\n/startattack\n\n\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast [nomod] Seed of Corruption\n/stopcasting [nomod]\n/cast [mod:alt] Seed of Corruption\n/startattack [nomod]\n\n### WEAKAURAS\nhttps://db.ascension.gg/?weakaura=1450.rev:1\n\n### NOTES\nPlease, don\'t do this with anything other than a troll—it would be heresy, and the Loa would come after you and kill your cat.', 'ability_racial_embraceoftheloa_bwonsomdi', 1, 1786257612, 1786257612, 2, 8, 0, 0, 1),
(170, '58d4977c-aa7d-4f32-a659-82cdfde9fabc', '', '', '', 10, 'Trix', 'My AOE/Hot for Fun.', '', '### OVERVIEW\nMy Build to have on file.\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nnone', 'ability_bossfelmagnaron_runeempowered', 1, 1786284079, 1786924717, 2, 4, 4, 0, 0),
(171, 'e53b42e5-671b-497a-b28a-f14bb92ef098', '', '', '', 10, 'Mangis', 'Test', '', '### OVERVIEW\nMeh', 'ability_deathknight_necroticaura', 0, 1786295735, 1786295735, 1, 8, 0, 0, 0),
(172, 'cabac109-0757-43a0-baca-60ce946c6110', '', '', '', 10, 'Pende', 'The Wild Huntsman', '', '### OVERVIEW\nA Feral Beastmaster empowered by Nature and the Elements\n\nThis build is a hybrid predator and beastmaster that fights alongside a heavily enhanced Tenacity pet. Instead of relying on burst windows or complex spellcasting, it wins through relentless sustained pressure, control, survivability, and almost zero downtime.\n\nThe pet initiates the fight and absorbs punishment while you shape-shift into Cat Form for damage or Bear Form for control and survival. Shaman enhancements keep passive damage rolling, while Hunter talents transform your companion into a terrifying frontline force. Druid utility gives you answers to virtually every situation.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\n* Extremely high uptime with Spirit Bond, Mend Pet, Rejuvenation, Frenzied Regeneration, and a durable Tenacity pet\n* Excellent solo leveling and elite quest capability\n* Pet can tank while you deal damage safely from Cat or Bear\n+ Strong single-target pressure through Rake, Rip, Cobra Strikes, Frenzy, Bestial Wrath, and The Beast Within\n+ Extremely safe against caster mobs thanks to Wind Shear, Bash, Intimidation, Feral Charge, and Roots\n+ Multiple defensive layers for difficult situations\n+ Strong passive damage from Lightning Shield, Thunder Hide, Flametongue Weapon, Corruption, and bleeds\n+ Virtually no downtime between pulls\n+ Flexible form usage with Cat for damage and Bear for control/survivability\n+ Powerful pet scaling through Beast Mastery, Unleashed Fury, Spirit Bond, Cobra Strikes, Frenzy, and Beast Mastery\n+ Excellent tracking utility for finding quest targets and farming efficiently\n+ Aspect of the Beast benefits both you and your pet while remaining active in forms\n+ Strong sustained damage rather than cooldown-dependent burst\n+ Multiple answers to almost every problem instead of relying on raw DPS\n+ Strong against elites, named mobs, and difficult quest encounters\n+ Great synergy between pet, bleeds, and mystic enchants\n+ Very thematic "Wild Huntsman" fantasy and playstyle\n\n- Highly dependent on pet uptime and pet survival\n- More keybinds and micromanagement than most leveling builds\n- Requires maintaining several buffs for peak performance\n- Damage is spread across many sources, making burst weaker than specialized builds\n- Not optimized for large-scale AoE farming\n- Cat bleed maintenance adds rotational complexity\n- Bear and Cat both have important uses, requiring form decisions during combat\n- Less raw Cat DPS than a dedicated Feral build\n- Less raw pet DPS than a pure glass-cannon Beast Mastery build\n- Several abilities and enchants compete for GCDs during difficult fights\n- Some power budget is invested into utility rather than direct damage\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nAgility>AP>Crit>Expertise>Hit>Haste>ArP>Stam>Int>SP\n\n### ROTATION\nKeep active:\n\nAspect of the Beast\nBest tracking for the area\nMark of the Wild\nThorns\nFlametongue Weapon\nLightning Shield / Thunder Hide\n\nStandard Mob\n\nPull\n1. Pet Attack\n2. Faerie Fire (Feral)\n3. Corruption (optional for tougher mobs)\n4. Shift to Cat\n\nCat Rotation\n1. Rake\n2. Claw\n3. Rip\nAfter that:\n\nContinue generating combo points.\nRefresh Rake.\nRefresh Rip if the mob somehow survives.\n\n\nMultiple Mobs\nPull\n1. Pet Attack and send to multiple targets\n2. Stampede\n4. Shift Cat\n\nCat Rotation\n1. Swipe\n2. Earthborer Acid on cooldowm\n3. Mend Pet as needed\n4. Thunderstomp from pet helps maintain control\n5. Pet attack on any target that switches to you - switch to Bear form if it becomes too much OR Dash around if safe to do so\n\nControl\n\nUse:\n\nBash\nIntimidation\nEntangling Roots\n\nElite Rotation\nPre-Pull\nEnsure all buffs active.\nFull pet health.\nBestial Wrath ready.\nFrenzied Regeneration ready.\nOpening\nPet Attack\nBestial Wrath\nIntimidation\nEarthborer Acid\nCorruption\nShift Cat\nFeral Charge\nDamage\nRake\nBuild combo points\nRip\nClaw generators\nControl\n\nPriority:\n\nWind Shear dangerous casts\nBash dangerous casts\nIntimidation\nRoots if reset needed\nEmergency\n\nIf things go wrong:\n\nShift Bear\nFrenzied Regeneration\nThunder Hide + Lightning Shield continue working\nLet pet recover threat\n\n\nCaster Mob\nPet Attack\nFeral Charge\nBash\nWind Shear major casts\nShift Cat\nNormal Cat rotation\n\nYour anti-caster kit:\n\nFeral Charge\nBash\nWind Shear\nIntimidation\n\nBestial Wrath Burst Window\n\nAgainst elites or difficult enemies:\n\nPet Attack\nBestial Wrath\nIntimidation\nEarthborer Acid\nFeral Charge\nRake\nRip\nContinue Cat rotation\n\nThis is your highest-pressure damage sequence because it stacks:\n\nBestial Wrath\nThe Beast Within\nCobra Strikes\nFrenzy\nUnleashed Fury\nPrimal Frenzy\nAgile Coordination\n\nall at roughly the same time.', 'ability_accretion', 0, 1786297890, 1786329802, 1, 8, 1, 0, 0),
(173, 'c9f0691b-93e6-4913-9cfa-b7069147efc9', '', '', '', 10, 'Idum', 'Stance Check Test !!!!', '', '### OVERVIEW\nYou have probly seen it before, 2 stances at once, but wich one stacks and wich one doesn\'t.\nProbly asked a lot around never getting a clear awnser, maby i have the awnser for you.\nThis build is made for testing wich Stance stack and those that don\'t.\n\nPS: not used for playing, Mistic Enchants not incleudid.\n\nI will spare you the details of finding out \n\nPRESENCE\nBlood and Unholy go with every stance exept other presences.\nFrost is concidert a tank stance, doesn\'t go with any other stance exept Mage and Warlock Mystic Enchant enhanced stances.\n\nFor the rest no other stance, shapeshift, tank buff or Mystic Enchantment enhanced Mage/Warlock armor can stack togetter.', 'ability_argus_soulbombdebuffsmall', 2, 1786298080, 1786313808, 2, 8, 0, 0, 0),
(174, '210e3e41-6168-4359-ab3f-3a98425d4fda', '', '', '', 10, 'Mazrek', 'frost mage sefl buffing', '', '### PROS_AND_CONS\nGood AOE good ST kinda mana starved', 'ability_deathknight_heartstopaura', 0, 1786315844, 1786315844, 2, 8, 3, 0, 0),
(175, 'e612e83a-fbf1-4dd7-bb12-56bddec9e549', '', '', '', 10, 'Idum', 'Idum\'s Frost Reaver', '', '### OVERVIEW\nThanks to good Mystic Enchants Frost Death Knighs can finaly properly tank.\n\nSpreading Plague\'s makes it good for AoE threat and Absolute Zero freeze them in place, stunning them, to give you a small opening.\nThis build is focus on Damage migration from cooldown spells moste used are Ice Barrier and Shamanistic Rage at higher level.\n\nWant to walk around like a Fortres of solid ice, Frost Reaver is your choise\nthese builds are still good for endgame.\n\nUpdate: Addit mastery bonusses, was forgotten.\n\n### PROS_AND_CONS\n|cff1aff1a+Many migration cooldowns and fast recoverd.|r\n+Good AoE thread by spreading plague\'s\n+Easy to Learn, tank for Beginner and Veterans \n\n-Mana controll low at lower level.\n-Lower on Damage\n-No 3th point this build is good\n\n### ITEMIZATION\nHit Rating 8% (-1% Heroic Presence) -> Defence Rating (Dodge/Parry) -> Stamina -> Critical Strike Rating -> Armor -> Attack Power\n\n### ROTATION\nActivate\n-----------\nSeal of Wisdom -> Mana Controll\nFrozen Mind -> Armor+\nMafe Armor -> Resistence\nFrost Presence -> Threat\n\nMigration\n-------------\nIce Barrier -> Each time it is off cooldown\nShamanist Rage -> Below 70% Mana\nIcebound Fortitude -> Panic Migraion at 30% HP or lower\nUnbreakable Armor -> Attack Power increasement and Armor, used at Berserker Phases at bosses to deal a bit more damage\nRunic Hurricane -> Ice Barrier not on time off cooldown\n\nAttacking\n------------\nIcy Touch + Plague Strike -> Frost Fever + Blood Plague upkeep\nRune Strike -> Rage consumption when able \nPestilence -> Spreading Frost Fever and Blood Plague\nAbsolute Zero -> AoE Controll in a group of 3 or more\nGalcial Spike -> Groep of range mobs to applied frost Fever\nIcy Shock -> Lost of Threat\n\n### MACROS\nRune Strike doesn\'t have a Global Cooldown.\nFor those that doesn\'t know what that mean, afther an attack skills have a 0.5 sec cooldown, made this way so that you can use every skill at once Rune Strike doesn\'t have that you can use it togetter with other skills.\n\n{HT}showtooltip\n/cast (moste used attack) Plague Strike\n/cast Runestrike', 'ability_mage_icewall', 2, 1786322694, 1787391594, 1, 2, 0, 0, 0);
